# FlowRat benchmarks.
#
# Run:  ./bench.sh
#
# Every figure is wall-clock time on the monotonic clock, taken over enough
# repetitions that the clock's resolution stops mattering, after a warm-up
# pass. Results are reported per step and per element so the scaling is
# readable without arithmetic, and a result that is used is always consumed
# by a printed number so the optimiser cannot delete the work.
#
# The rendering benchmark draws the real panels into a real framebuffer.
# Nothing here opens a window, so it measures drawing rather than the
# display's refresh.

